 drip,
 +dripping
of new files landing on my desk, just slightly too fast for me to keep up. By Wednesday, the papers had flooded the tabletop and started to overflow onto the floor, creating a halo of white around my workspace. Today, just two days later, my floor had become an ocean of papers, the piles stacked so high that any misstep would send everything tumbling down and drown me in papercuts. My speed reading and efficient use of abbreviations had done nothing to deter it, and despair was attempting to overcome me. 
 ->itch
 
 === itch ===
 The sight made my hand itch for a lighter, so I could return my office to its rightful state by any means necessary.
 +But I resisted.
 ->itch.whiteness
 +An itch I could not resist, a fire I could not stop.
 ->unstopable_fire
 
 =whiteness
 The stark whiteness invading every inch of my office was a cruel parody of everything I had worked tirelessly towards for the past month. Every memo, request, and itinerary littering my room was laughing at me: the employee stupid enough to think they could beat the system.
 ->goth
 
